course: dictionary
lesson: 16147
title: Wilting
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words describe how a thing looks and feels. Wilting describes something that droops and goes soft, like a plant with no water. When you meet wilting, read the words around it, because they are its context and they give clues.
explain: «The roses in the garden were wilting in the heat.» The roses are still there, but their petals and leaves hang down and look tired. Heat and no water are the clues, so wilting means drooping and going soft. Check it by swapping in your meaning: «The roses were drooping and going soft in the heat» still makes sense.
explain: Wilting can also describe people. «By noon the children were wilting in the sun» means they were getting tired and weak, not that they were falling over. Losing energy or confidence works too, as in «Her smile was wilting when the bad news came.»
fact: Wilting means drooping and going soft, often because a plant has not had enough water.
fact: In science, water pushes against plant cells and keeps them stiff; without it, the plant goes floppy and wilts.
fact: If a wilting plant is watered in time, it can perk up again.
fact: «Wilting» can describe a person who is getting tired or weak, especially in the heat.
fact: In stories, «wilting flowers» can stand for sadness or something coming to an end.
exercise: «The daisies were wilting because nobody had watered them.» What does wilting mean? | Growing taller every day | *Drooping and going soft for lack of water | Singing loudly | Shining brightly in the sun
exercise: «By the end of the match, the players were wilting in the heat.» What does wilting mean here? | Dancing happily | Running very fast | *Getting tired and weak | Cooling down with ice
exercise: Why does a plant wilt when it has no water? | It is too tall to stand up | Its leaves turn bright blue | *Water keeps its cells stiff, so without it the plant goes floppy
test: «Her smile was wilting as the bad news spread.» What does wilting suggest? | *Losing energy and confidence | Getting louder | Shining | Growing bigger
test: Which phrase describes a plant that needs water? | «Tall, strong trees» | «Fresh, cold rain» | «Bright, shining stars» | *«Wilting flowers»
exam: In «The wilting flower bent its head», what does wilting mean? | Laughing loudly | Glowing with light | Standing tall and proud | *Drooping and going soft
